    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.completion\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI currently have both Info and Signature set to 'single', as I like the break between my black background.\r\n\r\nShould this also include the drop down menu itself, or can you only add borders to the \"floating\" window with information?\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-10-08 at 17 31 53](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/beac77da-5324-41e1-9f39-0910ceaab013)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.2 Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.1727870382\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nConfigure mini.completion with following config:\r\n\r\n`return {\r\n    'echasnovski/mini.completion',\r\n    event = 'InsertEnter',\r\n    version = false,\r\n    config = function()\r\n        require('mini.completion').setup {\r\n            lsp_completion = { source_func = 'omnifunc', auto_setup = false },\r\n            window = {\r\n                info = { height = 25, width = 80, border = 'single' },\r\n                signature = { height = 25, width = 80, border = 'single' },\r\n            },\r\n        }\r\n    end\r\n}`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nthe drop down menu with string options would have a border option\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nCurrently with options in plugin there are no borders, so it blends into my background. ",
